        <body>
            <div xml:id="d95">

                <pb facs="0250" n="218" xml:id="pg218"/>

                <head>95. Memorandum From the Presidentʼs Special Assistant for National Security
                    Affairs (Bundy) to Secretary of State Rusk<anchor n="0" xml:id="d95-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1961-04-13">April 13,
                    1961</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The following decisions, of which you are already aware, are reported for
                    appropriate action: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>There will be no employment of U.S. armed forces against Cuba unless
                            quite new circumstances develop.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>The specific plan for paramilitary support, Nestor, has been rejected,
                            and the President does not wish further planning of any such operations
                            for an invasion of Cuba. There will be quiet disengagement from
                            associations developed in connection with Nestor.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">McGeorge Bundy</hi><anchor n="1"
                            xml:id="d95-f2"/></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
